    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n77983" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραζῶ</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>live by the side of</i> or <i>as an appendage to</i>, [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψυχὴ] τῷ σώματι παραζῶσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.672e
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> abs.,
				<i>live merely</i>, without doing anything, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὕτω παρέζων, κοὐκ ἔζων</span> I <i>was
				alive</i>, but lived not, <i><span class="en">
				Anaxandr.
				2.4
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζῆν, οὐ π. προσῆκε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.13a
				</span></i>
			.</div>
